* Lennard-Jones parameters for argon, krypton and xenon.
* NOT A CHARMM FILE. Split out of toppar_noble_gases_literature.str for
* read_cgenff_prm(path, append=True) via MMML_CGENFF_EXTRA_PRM; pairs with
* top_noble_gases_literature.rtf.
* Values are the classical 12-6 noble-gas parameters from the standard
* gas-transport / second-virial literature, converted to CHARMM's
* (epsilon, Rmin/2) convention with k_B = 0.0019872041 kcal/(mol K):
*   Ar  sigma 3.405 A  eps/k_B 119.8 K -> eps 0.23807 kcal/mol  Rmin/2 1.91099 A
*   Kr  sigma 3.600 A  eps/k_B 171.0 K -> eps 0.33981 kcal/mol  Rmin/2 2.02043 A
*   Xe  sigma 4.100 A  eps/k_B 221.0 K -> eps 0.43917 kcal/mol  Rmin/2 2.30105 A
* These are isolated-atom pair parameters. They were NOT fitted alongside
* CGenFF and are combined with it under Lorentz-Berthelot with no cross-term
* validation, so any noble-gas result in a MIXTURE is provisional. A PURE
* noble-gas box is the exception: every pair is like-like, so no cross term is
* involved and the numbers stand on their own.
* Full provenance and the comparison against the CHARMM He/Ne file and BMS:
* see toppar_noble_gases_literature.str.
* The single bare "*" below terminates the title. CHARMM ends the title at the
* FIRST such line and parses the rest as data, so there must be no other one.
*
ATOMS
MASS  -1  AR        39.94800 ! argon
MASS  -1  KR        83.79800 ! krypton
MASS  -1  XE       131.29300 ! xenon

NONBONDED nbxmod  5 atom cdiel fshift vatom vdistance vfswitch -
cutnb 14.0 ctofnb 12.0 ctonnb 10.0 eps 1.0 e14fac 1.0 wmin 1.5

AR     0.000000  -0.238070     1.910990
KR     0.000000  -0.339810     2.020430
XE     0.000000  -0.439170     2.301050

END
